---
source: crates/aidp-cli/tests/cli_surface.rs
expression: normalized
---
Git history as a differed signal: commit outcomes (revert, hotfix, success) derived from history, never from the reply envelope

Usage: <BIN> git [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  outcomes  Commit-by-commit verdicts (success | hotfixed | reverted) over the last 200 commits, via `aidp_core::gitlog`
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>
          Workspace to act on instead of the current directory

      --vault <PATH>
          Obsidian vault to use instead of `AIDP_VAULT`, `~/.aidp/config.json` or auto-detection

      --no-vault
          Ignore any vault and keep artefacts in the repo (`.aidp/pipelines/`)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Each command keeps its own default when omitted

          Possible values:
          - json-compact: One compact JSON document on a single line
          - json-pretty:  One indented JSON document
          - ndjson:       One compact JSON value per line
          - text:         Human-readable text
          - footer:       The one-line cost footer of a report, for `<BIN> cost ticket`; text elsewhere

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr; repeat for more (`-vv`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
